    "narrative": "The lineup for August 7th is headlined by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who sits as our clear elite option with an 80.53 score. Despite facing a left-hander, his power profile against Schultz remains top-tier, and his position in the three-hole provides the necessary RBI floor to anchor the roster. **Bryce Harper** (67.11) also provides significant upside against Soriano, as his advanced metrics (0.388 xwOBA) suggest he is primed to capitalize on a favorable matchup where the SP skill profile is negligible. **Jung Hoo Lee** (61.85) rounds out our high-efficiency tier; he benefits from a solid spot in the order and a favorable platoon advantage against Montero, making him a critical component for stabilizing our batting average while maintaining offensive volume.\n\nStrategic efficiency mandates a cautious approach with **Cal Raleigh** (41.12), who barely clears the threshold for active duty today. He is hampered by a difficult matchup against Rasmussen and a low spot in the batting order. The most difficult decision on the bench today was **Lawrence Butler** (43.97). While he offers more raw power than some starters, the negative dynamic platoon adjustment against Tolle\u2014combined with the need to prioritize higher-floor plate appearances\u2014pushed him to the bench. We are keeping a close eye on **Dylan Beavers**, who, despite a mediocre score of 44.61, remains in the lineup due to the scarcity of speed; however, his pairing against a high-end arm in Eovaldi represents a genuine risk to our efficiency targets.\n\nWe are avoiding the sub-40 floor with **Braden Montgomery**, whose profile failed to gain traction against a tough left-handed arm. While we monitor the ongoing status of **Yainer Diaz** and his 60.47 projection, we remain wary of the negative park factors impacting several of our bats. We are proceeding with this lineup to maximize daily caps, but should any late lineup changes affect **Jonathan Aranda** or **Masyn Winn**, we are prepared to shift to the bench reserves to ensure we are not sacrificing potential Roto gains against elite arms.",
